{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:5.90.110","page_type":"section"},"citation":"5.90.110","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.90.110","content_hash":"0f1c25aff5158db8d08742a401ab4f349e1f2ef003d7f9558990401be863a309","heading":"Application.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.90.110:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.90.110","text":"(a) Applicants for a license as a private security firm, or employee, agent or guard of a private security firm, shall file an application with the Chief of Police on forms to be prepared by the Chief of Police and supplied by the Police Department for that purpose. The application form shall ask, but not be limited to, the following:\n(1) If an applicant for a license as a private security firm:\n(i) The applicant’s name, address, race, sex, date of birth, telephone number and Social Security number;\n(ii) A description of the nature and type of business to be conducted;\n(iii) The services to be offered and the area expected to be covered in the conduct of the business; and\n(iv) A statement as to the number and type of vehicles to be used in the conduct of the business and a description thereof.\n(2) If an applicant for a license as an agent or an employee of a private security firm:\n(i) The applicant’s name, address, race, sex, date of birth, telephone number and Social Security number; and\n(ii) The name of the person or firm by whom the applicant is to be employed.\n(b) Each applicant as designated in subsection (a) of this section shall also file with the application:\n(1) A statement as to whether or not the applicant has been convicted of any of the crimes identified in TMC 5.90.140(a) within the time periods prescribed in that section;\n(2) A statement as to whether or not the applicant has had a judgment entered against the applicant for fraud, deceit or misrepresentation within 10 years immediately preceding the date of application and, if so, the details thereof; and\n(3) A statement as to the business or employment records of such applicant for the three years immediately preceding the date of application. (Ord. 20037 § 3, 12-6-16.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"d6ec8264-4add-525e-8372-9056ccd0947d"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.90.110","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.90.110","content_hash":"46180c243c4532079784e2643f21818d028f4f08b55d0cbadd051a5c5b287713","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.90.110:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.90.110:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.90.110","text":"(a) Applicants for a license as a private security firm, or employee, agent or guard of a private security firm, shall file an application with the Chief of Police on forms to be prepared by the Chief of Police and supplied by the Police Department for that purpose. The application form shall ask, but not be limited to, the following:","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"426030b8-a785-576f-8803-7dd2f1bce40a"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"5.90.110","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.90.110","content_hash":"a5d6ff5554692e6d31c0748967ec59ce543d4bf915e8e7e890ed26d8dd755c09","heading":null,"ordinal":1,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.90.110:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:5.90.110:block:1","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/5.90.110","text":"(1) If an applicant for a license as a private security firm:","type":"paragr